        "comments": "The assembly of Arnoglossus thori (fArnTho1) is based on 76X ONT data and 90X Arima Hi-C data generated as part of the ATLASea programme (https://www.atlasea.fr). The assembly process included the following steps: initial ONT+HiC assembly generation with Hifiasm, removal of contaminant sequences using Context, and Hi-C-based scaffolding with YaHS of each haplotype. No contigs were found to be contaminants (bacterial, archaeal, or viral). Mitochondrial genome was assembled using ptGAUL. Finally, Both haplotypes were analyzed and manually improved using Pretext. During manual curation, 32 haplotypic regions were removed, totaling 9.646Mb (with the largest being 1.497Mb). Chromosome-scale scaffolds confirmed by Hi-C data were named in order of size.",
